{
  "body" : "CONTENT BRIEF\nDraw {{subject}} in {{setting}}, arranged {{orientation}}. Keep the subject specific and readable through its outline and a few essential interior marks; include no lettering. Add a small handwritten artist signature: \"{{signature}}\".\n\nSTYLE DIRECTION\nUse a sparse black contour drawing on a clean white ground: thin, slightly wavering hand-drawn lines; occasional doubled or lightly ghosted gray strokes; large unfilled white shapes; and a few tiny broken marks. Keep contours mostly crisp but imperfect, with restrained, uneven line weight ({{line_weight}}). Use black as the sole strong color, faint cool gray only as incidental sketch echoes, and no filled color areas. Suggest depth through overlapping outlines and sparse interior contours rather than tonal shading; keep lighting neutral and shadows absent. Preserve a raw, minimal pen-sketch surface without paper grain, paint, or polished vector smoothing.\n\nDESIGN RULES\nUse a portrait canvas, with the main form large, vertically dominant, and centrally weighted; let it approach or pass beyond some frame edges while retaining generous white space around the upper focal area. Keep secondary context low-detail and subordinate, with clear separation from the main silhouette. Preserve an airy, asymmetrical rhythm of broad blank regions and long, loose contour sweeps regardless of subject.\n\nAVOID\nAvoid color fills, gradients, dense crosshatching, realistic tonal rendering, uniform mechanical vector lines, decorative borders, busy scenery, and centered typography.\n\nAdditional constraints: {{extra}}\n\nVariables: {{subject}}, {{setting}}, {{orientation}}, {{line_weight}}, {{extra}}",
